text:
That's a clean first run: the face node is running (spirit-face, starts at boot), it minted its invite, joined your relay as 'face', and accepts your node. It stopped where it should, at Caddy. Next, in this order:
1) ON YOUR BOX, in your SpiritOS checkout: git pull, then
   node bash/face-owner.js MCowBQYDK2VwAyEAdcWPg2Id8YU/9+42YYSCNEl9KRUYSlnukXc6RmtQ824=
   (the face node's key from your output).
2) ON spirit-3: open /etc/caddy/Caddyfile and put these 5 lines at the very top, above 'import sites/*.caddy':
{
	on_demand_tls {
		ask http://127.0.0.1:65434/.well-known/spirit-name
	}
}
   then: caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile --adapter caddyfile && systemctl reload caddy && /root/face/SpiritOS/bash/face-tls
   Its last line should say join.face.spirit.andyflinn.com 'is a real name'. That's why step 1 comes first.
3) From anywhere: curl -sS https://join.face.spirit.andyflinn.com/ should give 501 last-leg-not-built with your key.
